  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pacific Detector Dog Programme 2025-2030: Phase 2</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Pacific Detector Dog Programme (PDDP) builds&#xa0;detection capability in the Detector Dog Units of border agencies&#xa0;in the Cook Islands, Tonga, Samoa and Fiji. The programme provides trained dogs, and builds capability in dog handling,&#xa0;leadership,&#xa0;systems and processes, and investigation and&#xa0;use of legal powers to enforce and prosecute intercepts of illicit material, primarily drugs.&#xa0;PDDP is implemented by NZ Police, and jointly with NZ Customs in Fiji and Samoa.</narrative>
  </description>
